<article class="env-lemma" id="04IR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04IR">Lemma <span data-tag="04IR">7.30.6</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. If $s : \mathcal{G} \to \mathcal{F}$ is a morphism of sheaves on $\mathcal{C}$ then there exists a natural commutative diagram of morphisms of topoi </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})/\mathcal{G} \ar[rd]_{j_\mathcal {G}} \ar[rr]_ j &  &  \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})/\mathcal{F} \ar[ld]^{j_\mathcal {F}} \\  &  \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}) &  }  \]
</div>
  <p> where $j = j_{\mathcal{G}/\mathcal{F}}$ is the localization of the topos $\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})/\mathcal{F}$ at the object $\mathcal{G}/\mathcal{F}$. In particular we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  j^{-1}(\mathcal{H} \to \mathcal{F}) = (\mathcal{H} \times _\mathcal {F} \mathcal{G} \to \mathcal{G})  \]
</div>
  <p> and </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  j_!(\mathcal{E} \xrightarrow {e} \mathcal{G}) = (\mathcal{E} \xrightarrow {s \circ e} \mathcal{F}).  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The description of $j^{-1}$ and $j_!$ comes from the description of those functors in Lemma <a href="/tag/04GZ" data-tag="04GZ">7.30.1</a>. The equality of functors $j_{\mathcal{G}!} = j_{\mathcal{F}!} \circ j_!$ is clear from the description of these functors (as forgetful functors). By adjointness we also obtain the equalities $j_\mathcal {G}^{-1} = j^{-1} \circ j_\mathcal {F}^{-1}$, and $j_{\mathcal{G}, *} = j_{\mathcal{F}, *} \circ j_*$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>